  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN"># quick win initiatives under the PIP</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Initiation plan</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Judicial training mechanism will be improved, assessment reports on Judicial mapping and geographical rezoning get prepared; 
2. Gender auditing of federal courts judges and staff will be undertaken; assessment reports shall be produced on women court users; female court users supported as per recommendation of the assessment; work Place Anti- harassment and Anti-Discrimination Policy ill be developed; Mentoring and Coaching Program Toolkit developed; 
3. public relations of Courts strengthened/Communication strategies developed; Legal and Justice Clubs in Primary and Secondary Schools established; awareness on Rule of law and the role of courts in promoting justice, human rights and democracy created; assessment report on ADR/feasibility of Mandatory out of Court Dispute Resolution produced</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Research and studies aimed at improved at Judicial training mechanism were conducted. An assessment of the existing training curriculum was conducted the findings and recommendations of which serve as inputs for improving the system. Training strategy and curriculum were also developed. 
2. Public legal awareness and transparency of federal judiciary enhanced through programs on access to justice, rule of law and various legal issues that were aired on public TV. 
3. Court Annexed Mediation strengthened through support provided for the establishment and strengthening of Offices in Addis Ababa to increase efficiency of courts increasing access to justice of citizens.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Two national experts supported the FSC and LJAAC;assessment reports on the existing judicial training mechanism conducted, curriculums and training modules designed, judicial training programs conducted;backlog reduction at Federal Courts reduced;Judicial Reform Project office equipped/established; 2 public relations and communication experts deployed, Communication strategies developed, 3 sets of audio-visual sets of equipment for PR offices, # of awareness creation programs; Assessment report, training module on Mandatory out of Court Dispute Resolution produced; Court Annexed Mediation Officer deployed, office equipped; Number of cases settled by mediation</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Operational capacity and efficiency of the judiciary enhanced; Transparency of the Judiciary and access to justice enhanced; Alternative Dispute Resolution mechanisms strengthened</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. assessment reports on Judicial mapping and geographical rezoning; Gender auditing of federal courts judges and staff undertaken; assessment reports produced on women court users; female court users supported as per recommendation of the assessment; Work Place Anti- harassment and Anti-Discrimination Policy developed; Mentoring and Coaching Program Toolkit developed; 
2. Mandatory out of Court Dispute Resolution strengthened; support to female court users provided; trainings, workshops, publications on GBV related activities undertaken; Joint-Justice assessment and formulation of a broad programming framework completed.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
